WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.839 --> 00:00:11.302
I've been working for, you know,

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:13.282
15 years as a stunt performer on

00:00:13.282 --> 00:00:15.185
a variety of sets all over the world.

00:00:15.185 --> 00:00:17.529
Majority of the day is
you're fighting and falling.

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:19.679
"Atomic Blonde"...

00:00:19.679 --> 00:00:21.200
I am so proud of that movie.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.052
So, we had this stairwell
scene, this fight,

00:00:23.052 --> 00:00:25.938
that in the script was,
she shoots two guys.

00:00:25.938 --> 00:00:27.705
But, you know, we were talking
to Dave and we were like,

00:00:27.705 --> 00:00:31.704
"Hey, you know, what if we
do this epic fight scene?"

00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:33.906
We actually went to the
stairwell and we shot it

00:00:33.906 --> 00:00:36.424
how we would shoot it on set.

00:00:36.424 --> 00:00:38.479
So, we call this a previs, a stunt previs,

00:00:38.479 --> 00:00:40.738
and then we have Charlize go in and

00:00:40.738 --> 00:00:42.972
shoot the first section until it was good,

00:00:42.972 --> 00:00:45.707
sometimes 15 to 20 takes for each section,

00:00:45.707 --> 00:00:47.267
because it had to be perfect.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.116
They put me in when it was the -

00:00:48.116 --> 00:00:49.599
you know, throwing -

00:00:49.599 --> 00:00:50.532
getting thrown down the stairs,

00:00:50.532 --> 00:00:52.057
and getting thrown into the wall,

00:00:52.057 --> 00:00:53.930
and then back to Charlize's section.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.194
I'm so proud of that sequence.

00:00:55.194 --> 00:00:57.660
I think we really accomplished
something incredible.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.310
She's beautiful, but she is tough.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.426
She wants to be good.

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:01.759
She wants to do everything.

00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:04.889
And she was there, all the
time, in the gym with us,

00:01:04.889 --> 00:01:06.984
and you know, the Tom Cruises
and the Angelina Jolies

00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:08.180
and Charlize and Keanu, like,

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.960
they're all very athletic
and very talented.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.642
The problem is they can't
do all their own stunts

00:01:13.642 --> 00:01:16.617
because of liability,
and, you know, you can't -

00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:17.874
just can't do that.

00:01:17.874 --> 00:01:21.496
I get excited, but I'm not
nervous, I don't fear the stunt.

00:01:21.496 --> 00:01:23.389
And I just go through
the stunt in my mind.

00:01:23.389 --> 00:01:25.067
I make sure everything -
all the rigging looks good.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.340
And then you just go,
"Okay, cool, call action."

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.607
Like, "I'm ready, let's do this."

00:01:41.695 --> 00:01:43.878
So, I probably worked for
10 years without my family

00:01:43.878 --> 00:01:45.448
really knowing what I was doing.

00:01:45.448 --> 00:01:48.068
Now my mom works in film,
though, so she sees everything.

00:01:48.068 --> 00:01:49.801
She once brought me my grenade launcher.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.509
That was pretty hilarious.

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:53.552
Like, "Mom, I need my grenade launcher!"

00:01:55.527 --> 00:01:57.908
My story is I was modeling,

00:01:57.908 --> 00:02:00.355
and so, all the models
were taking acting classes,

00:02:00.355 --> 00:02:02.753
and they were, you know,
being extras on set

00:02:02.753 --> 00:02:04.178
to make extra money.

00:02:04.178 --> 00:02:06.350
And I saw this girl roll down some stairs,

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.424
and shoot some guns,
and beat up some dudes,

00:02:08.424 --> 00:02:11.081
and I was like, "I want to do that."

00:02:11.081 --> 00:02:14.317
You know, most of my training
was in the park by myself,

00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:15.925
running and falling

00:02:15.925 --> 00:02:17.400
over and over and over again

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.194
until it felt natural.

00:02:20.194 --> 00:02:22.894
I have probably fallen thousands of times.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:27.427
Sometimes I am the only woman in the room.

00:02:27.427 --> 00:02:30.778
There's definitely a
lack of female leadership

00:02:30.778 --> 00:02:32.820
in our stunt industry.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.028
So, you know, you're falling,

00:02:34.028 --> 00:02:35.903
but you're falling in
a skirt all the time.

00:02:35.903 --> 00:02:37.888
You know, I go into
the costumes, and I go,

00:02:37.888 --> 00:02:40.873
"No skirts. We're going to do pants now."

00:02:40.873 --> 00:02:43.157
But I think it's changing,
and I was the first

00:02:43.157 --> 00:02:45.596
female stunt coordinator
that Marvel has hired.

00:02:45.596 --> 00:02:48.641
As a stunt coordinator, you're
taking on the responsibility

00:02:48.641 --> 00:02:50.391
of designing all the
action, the stunt action,

00:02:50.391 --> 00:02:52.387
making sure it's as safe as possible,

00:02:52.387 --> 00:02:54.606
and then coming up with
some really creative way

00:02:54.606 --> 00:02:57.689
to tell the story through action.

00:02:57.689 --> 00:03:01.708
The riskiest stunt, I think,
that I've done is in -

00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:02.994
we were shooting in Bulgaria,

00:03:02.994 --> 00:03:07.131
and I was driving a two-horse
chariot at a full gallop.

00:03:07.131 --> 00:03:09.736
I had to jump from the
chariot to the horse

00:03:09.736 --> 00:03:11.502
and it was just me in the chariot.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.787
That one got me going like, "Whew, okay."

00:03:16.787 --> 00:03:19.803
As soon as they call action,
you just, you have to commit.

